KACZYNSKI BOUNDARY REFRAME: G(t)=t(log Pi)' is analytic in the disk |t|<1/rho; the
saddle values t_j=1/w_j are BOUNDARY SINGULARITIES on |t|=1/rho. TNC <=> G constant <=>
the boundary function (radial limits, one per branch = 'approach label') is TRIVIAL <=>
empty singular set <=> R monomial. The branches u_i(t) ARE Kaczynski's approach paths.
